WEBVTT

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:28.150
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.730 --> 00:02:02.150
The Retriever
Chapter III

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.790
Imperial Year 484, January 1st...

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:15.250
...the cruiser, Hershrichlenchen, under the command of Commander Reinhard von Musel...

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:17.780
...watched New Year's Day
arrive inside Alliance territory.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.320
Needless to say, they had no time to
celebrate the New Year behind enemy lines.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:40.110
Can't the equipment in
question be moved to this ship ?

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:44.800
Its control computer is linked
to the ship's main computer...

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.410
...and to disconnect it,
we need the access code.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:52.800
The way things are going, should we give up on retrieving it and destroy it instead ?

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.750
We can't do that !

00:02:56.250 --> 00:03:00.570
Yes, our orders were to either
retrieve the equipment or destroy it...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.250
...but the data results of
all previous experiments...

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:08.550
...are in the test unit's memory, and a backup does not exist.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.800
Since we can't read the data...

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.500
...we have no choice but to retrieve all the equipment, along with the ship.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.250
We were not able to
capture Helksheimer alive.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.030
If we can at least salvage the 
equipment, then that'd be for the best.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.100
Moreover...

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:35.400
...um, no, but is there any way to find out the access code ?

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.280
It seems Helksheimer's
daughter knows it, but...

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:46.050
Lieutenant Junior Grade,
what's the daughter's condition ?

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:46.920
Well...

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.750
So you know the access code, correct ?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.280
I do.

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.240
Then would you please tell us ?

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:56.450
I refuse.

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:00.040
I have no reason to tell you,
since you are my father's enemies.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:06.320
I'm sorry about your father.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.860
But, um, he died in an accident.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.900
Even so, he wouldn't have 
died if you hadn't attacked us !

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.510
We were only trying
to secure his person.

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.220
That's the same thing !

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.610
After all, she's only
a ten year old child.

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:38.580
We can't torture her
or use truth serum.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.950
Oh, even you think that ?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:44.150
P...please don't misunderstand me.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:44.700
I'm...

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.220
Captain, please return
to the bridge immediately.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:48.960
What has happened ?

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.550
We've detected what appears to be an
enemy patrol unit approaching this area.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.250
I understand.
I'm on my way.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.820
Just as you've heard.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:59.890
We can't stay here for long.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.170
For the time being, we'll prepare to take the ship along with us.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:07.380
LTJG Kircheis, continue to
command the other ship.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.540
Lt. Commander Bendling, focus on analyzing the system, and keep trying to access it.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:15.860
Are there any questions ?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.900
Since we must move,
where should we go ?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:24.870
The route data we just obtained from the other ship is only for this area, isn't it ?

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.900
The Phezzani side
seems to be cautious...

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:30.710
...and they only gave us data from
the Corridor to the next port of call.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.550
Since we don't have
data for a new route...

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:38.800
...we have no choice but to
return on the route we used.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:47.550
Report.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.000
They're clearly heading 
toward this group of comets.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:55.000
Since there are no other
hiding places in the vicinity...

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.550
...it's only natural that they would be suspicious of this area.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.880
It's only a matter of time
before they discover us.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:06.520
Rather than continuing to hide, it's 
probably better to plan a quick departure.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:08.170
Is the other ship prepared ?

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:08.940
It's ready.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.200
Good.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.350
We'll depart, camouflaging ourselves within the movement of the comet.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.800
Report on the enemy's movement.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:33.660
They've spread out, and are starting to investigate the star system.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.760
That was a close call.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.170
Wait please.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.230
One enemy ship is following us !

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:43.350
They must have found us.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:50.090
No, since it's only one ship, they're trying to make sure that we're a comet, just in case.

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:54.230
Once they get closer, it'll be
obvious that we're not a comet.

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:01.680
Is it possible to establish 
communications with LTJG Kircheis ?

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.930
The communication systems are still being repaired, but at this distance...

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.730
...we can definitely establish
communications via laser link.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.350
Good. Make it so.

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:15.550
...is what we plan to do.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:18.690
As soon as you're ready, use
a light signal and let me know.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.050
Roger.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.450
I wonder if we can
pull this off, though.

00:07:23.450 --> 00:07:26.580
It hinges on whether or not we can
buy ourselves enough time to prepare.

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:34.680
The enemy ship is still approaching !

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.660
Is it ready yet ?

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.050
Still no signal.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.710
The enemy ship is accelerating !

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:50.950
They must have noticed.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.070
It appears so.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.050
A message from the enemy ship -
they're ordering us to heave to.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.490
Ignore it.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:00.090
Aren't you ready yet, Kircheis ?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.900
Light signal has been confirmed.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:04.640
Good.

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:06.870
Tell the enemy ship
that we're complying.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.300
Reduce speed by 1/2.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:22.350
Enemy ship, still approaching.

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.180
Distance, 7,000.

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.810
Maintain course and lure
them within close range.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.790
They're requesting
communications, but...

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:30.650
Pretend that our communication system isn't working well.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:36.050
Enemy ship is advancing toward us.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:37.030
What's their distance ?

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.560
It'll be 5,000 shortly.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:39.330
Kircheis !

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:40.370
Now !

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.380
Release Seffle particles.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:20.800
Good.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:21.560
Accelerate immediately !

00:09:26.950 --> 00:09:30.660
Warning from the enemy ship - they're
saying they'll destroy us if we don't heave to.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:31.950
Ignore them.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.230
The enemy ship is accelerating !

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.350
Brilliant !

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:06.020
Even if we can't control their
direction, we can still use them.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:09.350
But with this, the enemy has 
become aware of our presence.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.940
The other ships will pursue us.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.050
Hurry up and withdraw.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:12.850
Yes, sir !

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:20.680
Was it because of this escape plan that you didn't consent to destroy the equipment ?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:26.700
With normal Seffle Particles,
usage is limited to what we just did.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.820
But it's still better than nothing.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:31.250
If we could use directional Seffle Particles...

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.690
...do you think we can escape even
if we're completely surrounded ?

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.450
I'm somewhat hoping for that.

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:42.090
I hope we'll find out the access code for that reason as well.

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:58.750
You left my father where he was ?

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:01.800
We don't have any other
place to secure him...

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.290
...and the capsule is suitable
for preserving his body.

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.870
I feel sorry for him...

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:38.700
These others followed my
father to the end, but...

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.600
Where is your mother ?

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:49.000
She died last month.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.400
She was poisoned...

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.410
...by someone.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:02.360
My father and I 
just barely escaped.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.650
That's why my father
decided to defect.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.920
But...

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.300
This was left in your capsule.

00:12:35.300 --> 00:12:36.750
It's precious to you, isn't it ?

00:12:38.550 --> 00:12:41.920
My father and mother gave it to me.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:44.000
Are you going to return it to me ?

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.400
Then we'll have to
handle it with care.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:48.820
We won't take it away from you.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:53.950
But you're going to confiscate the money my father took with him, aren't you ?

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:03.300
No, I was ordered to retrieve the military's top secret equipment...

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.020
...not to confiscate his private assets.

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:12.000
Isn't it customary for you to plunder them as a privilege of the ones assigned to the mission ?

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:17.850
Um, things like that seem to happen at times, but that's only what shameless people do...

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:20.590
...it's not what honorable
Imperial military officers do.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.090
We're not space pirates.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:31.660
Besides, such actions are what our captain detests the most.

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.150
Is that so ?

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.960
I guarantee it.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.880
You can trust me.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:53.110
You two don't seem like bad people.

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:14.060
Pursued by the Alliance fleet, Reinhard headed toward the Iserlohn Corridor, retracing their earlier route.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:19.710
We've intercepted an
enemy transmission.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:23.700
More than 10 enemy ships appear
to be deployed along the route ahead.

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:25.150
It seems to be a patrol unit.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.080
The route has been blockaded ?

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.220
We have no choice.

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:30.100
Make a turn in the 4 o'clock direction.

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.650
We'll head toward the binary star area we talked about.

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:35.310
Are we taking shelter 
inside the asteroid field ?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:36.490
That's one reason.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:39.390
But we'll also eliminate our pursuers.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.250
Contact LTJG Kircheis.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:43.550
We'll use the Seffle Particles again.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:44.690
This time at maximum output.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:15:00.000
The gap between us and
the enemy is closing.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:01.750
That's fine.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:04.140
Let Helksheimer's ship sail ahead of us.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:07.730
Have them keep releasing Seffle Particles in front of our ship.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:12.820
Captain, if we do that, we will all be dead when the enemy fires at us.

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:15.230
That is if they attack us.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:16.490
But the enemy won't be firing.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:21.050
The enemy's intention is
to seize the equipment.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:22.710
That's right.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:27.090
Moreover, unlike the last time, 
they're well aware of the situation.

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:31.500
If they attack this ship,
Helksheimer's ship will be destroyed, too.

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.090
This way, they can't fire at us.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:55.100
Hey, won't the engines
ignite the Seffle Particles ?

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.160
Aren't you confusing it 
with gas and stuff like that ?

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:03.250
They only ignite with high heat,
like lasers or beam cannons.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:04.450
I see.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:05.550
Communications !

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:10.150
For their sake, send a
warning to the enemy ship...

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.130
...that the area is saturated
with Seffle Particles.

00:16:14.050 --> 00:16:14.600
Yes, sir !

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:21.050
The enemy ships are accelerating, keeping their course.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:23.260
Just as I expected.

00:16:23.260 --> 00:16:25.260
We'll drag them into
the asteroid field !

00:16:42.490 --> 00:16:45.500
They're trying to get 
ahead{of this ship} and separate us{i.e. Reinhard's ship and Helksheimer's ship}.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.510
Don't let them get ahead.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:47.800
We'll sail on parallel courses.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.350
Avoiding the asteroids,
sail at maximum output !

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.740
Captain, this situation is dangerous.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:22.530
I know.

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:24.800
Kircheis.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.350
Stop the Seffle Particles.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:33.710
The Seffle Particles have been cut off.

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.370
Now, ram the enemy ship !

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:50.450
Withdraw !

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:20.470
If the Seffle Particles hadn't been cut off,
we would have been caught in the explosion.

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.440
The particles were cut 
off at the perfect time.

00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:25.540
LTJG Kircheis is truly brilliant.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.500
But what do we do now ?

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.440
This route has been completely blocked.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:40.250
This is where we initially made contact with the Imperial Military Liaison Officer at Phezzan, isn't it ?

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.540
That's right.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:44.630
Let's try to establish contact again.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.550
We're getting something !

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.000
Fix the coordinates.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:54.380
Can you communicate ?

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.190
Video or audio communication is risky.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:00.230
I would think an encrypted message is the best we can manage.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:01.620
It can't be helped.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.800
Let them know our situation.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:07.800
We have a response.

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:12.500
Captain, the Military Liaison Officer
sent us an alternate navigation route.

00:19:15.510 --> 00:19:17.900
Well, this is more than I expected.

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.170
There are many problems.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:23.070
The route data on which this plan is based is incomplete.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:29.600
Also, it's a long detour, and we won't make
it to the Fortress without resupplying.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:33.310
The Military Liaison Officer
seems to be aware of that, too.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:37.170
He says he'll request 
resupply from the homeland.

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:40.050
I wonder if we can rely on that.

00:19:40.050 --> 00:19:41.800
Can you confirm ?

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.750
Communications have broken off again.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:57.550
Captain, there is something
I'd like to consult you on.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.850
...is what happened.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.700
I knew there was some 
hidden purpose behind all this...

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:18.890
...but there seems to be circumstances that are more complicated than I initially thought.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:25.840
I suspect such information might be included in the computer data in question{i.e. the one that they can't access}.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:28.940
Do you think Lt. Commander Bendling knows about it ?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.900
I can't tell if he knows the
contents of the information...

00:20:31.900 --> 00:20:38.610
...but I would think he's aware of its existence and has been ordered to retrieve it.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:40.410
But...

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:44.700
...he doesn't seem to know the
hidden circumstances of the affair...

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:48.210
...and appeared shaken when he heard Lady Margareta's story.

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:56.890
I don't know if it will do any good to take Lady Margareta back to the homeland.

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:59.710
Considering her age, I doubt she'd
be held accountable for the crime...

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:02.780
...but because of it, she might
become the target of assassination.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.600
She probably has distant relatives...

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:08.250
...but they'll fear getting involved,
and none will be likely to adopt her.

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:10.920
Then what do you
think we should do ?

00:21:10.920 --> 00:21:13.080
How about if we
make a deal with her ?

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.590
A deal ?

00:21:15.590 --> 00:21:17.250
With a ten year old child ?

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.370
Lord Reinhard...

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:24.110
...how old were you when
you made your resolution ?

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.350
All right.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.210
But what exactly do we do ?

00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:35.950
First, we learn the access code from her, and in exchange for the equipment in question...

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:38.790
...we return the ship and its assets to her.

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:41.440
You mean we let her defect from here ?

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:46.960
But even if we return the assets to her, unless she has a trustworthy guardian of some sort...

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:49.300
...I wonder if she'll be able
to continue on safely.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:51.900
That's...right.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:57.350
Moreover, for that deal, she'll need to tell us the access code first...

00:21:57.350 --> 00:22:00.320
...but I wonder if she'll
trust us and comply.

00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:03.350
I will take full responsibility for persuading her on that point.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.030
Let me think about it.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:14.160
Without making a decision, Reinhard led the ships to depart once again.

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:19.450
Based on the new navigational data,
he took the alternate route to avoid ambushes.

00:22:39.930 --> 00:22:44.230
With this maneuver, they were able to
evade the enemy for the time being.

00:22:44.230 --> 00:22:48.880
But it was obvious that they had no choice
but to proceed toward Iserlohn Corridor...

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:53.050
...so the Alliance would naturally
blockade the vicinity of the Corridor.

00:22:53.940 --> 00:22:56.100
Is there a means
to break through ?

00:22:56.800 --> 00:22:59.950
The situation continued to pose challenges.

00:22:59.950 --> 00:23:03.800
To be continued

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:14.470
[ The Promised Future ]

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:14.470
End Theme

00:23:09.470 --> 00:23:14.470
Vocals: Ogura Kei

